{"text": "BROWN & WILLIAMSON TOBACCO CORPORATION\nRESEARCH, DEVELOPMENT & ENGINEERING\n\nINTERNAL CORRESPONDENCE\n\nTo: Mr. B. J. Martines\ncc: Mr, M. L. Reynolds\nDr. PL. Aulbach\nFROM: Mr. C. F. Gregory\nDATE: September 6, 1984\n\nSUBJECT: KENT 100 ~ CKILE/922\n\nThe Following changes in the KENT 100 product from Chile have beea\nrequested for economical reasons and for rationalization of different\nmaterials:\n\nFROM 0.\n\nTow 3.9/39,000 ANCEL \u20143.9/41,000 KODAK or AMCEL\nNet Tobacco Weight Control 2%\n\nAnalytical and physical data for samples MW-1 control and test are\nattached.\n\nTobacco net weight reduction targeted at 2% went from 914 mg to\n901 mg/eig, a 1.42% reduction. Pressure drops of the control and test\n\nsamples were similar, Tar and micotine were reduced slightly in the\ntest sample.\n\nCIA\ncre\ncrores\noss\n\nAttachment\n\n620781808",
